  <iati-identifier>XI-IATI-EC_INTPA-2022-PC-24290</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening civic space to resist disinformation and harmful narratives in Sri Lanka and the Maldives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall Objective&lt;/strong&gt;: &quot;a resilient and inclusive civic space that promotes and protects human rights, fundamental freedoms and democracy in Sri Lanka and in the Maldives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific Objective:&lt;/strong&gt; HRDs, CSOs and independent media promote fundamental freedoms and push for a widened civic space online and offline, enhancing Sri Lankan and Maldivian audiences with access to relevant and reliable information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;More specifically this 24 months Action aims to enhance Sri Lankan and Maldivian audiences&#xbf; access to relevant and reliable information by strengthening literacy of civil society and media to detect and counter disinformation and hate speech and allow for pluralist voices to be heard online and offline which upholds fundamental freedoms. The Action rests on the assumption that capacitating media and CSOs with tools and approaches to detect, counter and cover harmful narratives and safeguarding content providers against emerging threats will result in robust space for public interest information to be produced and distributed to the benefit of the Sri Lanka and Maldivian people.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three Outcome&lt;/strong&gt;s, focusing on 1) the skills and capacities of CSOs, HRDs, journalists and media to produce and distribute content that counters disinformation and hate speech; 2) safety and protection measures for journalists and other content producers, and 3) strengthening operational and financial capacity of partner and expand its operations to the Maldives, have been identified for this purpose.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
